{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/463384-open-source-poll","id":463384,"title":"Open Source Poll?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-31T06:03:04-07:00","id":463384,"title":"Open Source Poll?","content":"Just a Poll...<br /> <br /> Do you think that the Onyx Path should take one of their existing game mechanics and make it open source if so which one?<br /> <br /> Do you think that the Onyx Path should make a open source game mechanics in the future?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T07:20:41-07:00","id":463487,"title":"","content":"No.4567890","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T08:50:12-07:00","id":463591,"title":"","content":"No. <br /> <br /> If a system is good/popular/usable it's contrary to the interests of the company/owner to do so.<br /> <br /> If a system is not good, it's not going to spread.<br /> <br /> Open or closed, nothing prevents individuals from using the rules in other settings for their own consumption, If closed and copyrighted all you have to do is make reference to those books that have the mechanics and creating and freely releasing whole new settings that use them. <br /> <br /> I have only seen two situations where there was an advantage to freely offering the ruleset. First to get approval from people that hold that anything open is clearly superior to anything sold by The Man. Second was to circumvent legal ownership when the people were convinced that the ruleset was going to be locked down and it's use forbidden by legal means from new owners. And the second one came to bite the owners in the ass rather badly.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the case of OPP, I have not seen anything like the demand or interest in the rule systems to even justify considering it. Is there a large market clamoring to run other games on the Scion engine? Trinity? On the beta engine for Cavaliers of Mars? They don't own anything else apart from a system for the next set of Trinity and Scion games that is still being worked on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T11:49:07-07:00","id":463683,"title":"","content":"The number of fan games made for the nWOD, and fan material done for cWOD, Exalted, and Scion... basically means that fans that want to write stuff will.<br /> <br /> Also... OP doesn't have their own system yet; even if the Sardonyx one is in process to become it. They don't have a choice about the WOD and Exalted systems (those are owned by CCP), and Cavaliers of Mars and Pugmire are going to be based on other systems.<br /> <br /> But basically, open source systems only really benefit game companies who are mostly focused on producing an &quot;engine&quot; and are looking towards other people to create setting content with their engine (aka Fate). OP makes complete packages of engine + setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T07:06:04-07:00","id":464645,"title":"","content":"Open source never seems to go well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T13:17:05-07:00","id":465076,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure that's accurate. But as I said before, it really seems to work well for publishers looking to get an engine out there more than a complete game. There's enough people out there will to pay people that put out an open source engine even though they can get it for free; if the engine gets used in games they like. The Fate Core/FAE Kickstarter did wonderful for a PWYW product, because people like the games made with Fate (often not be Evil Hat), and they're willing to fund new Fate rules, which means those other games they like get improved rules with it.<br /> <br /> Open source backfired on WotC (pretty much letting Pathfinder take D&amp;D down to tied for market share), and I think CCP would be in the same boat if they opened up the ST-base systems, but it is a very different place to be starting from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}